#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:3
msgid "How to Migrate from RustRover to Zed"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:5
msgid ""
"This guide covers keybindings, settings, and the differences you'll "
"encounter as a Rust developer switching from RustRover."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:7
msgid "Install Zed"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:9
msgid "Zed is available on macOS, Windows, and Linux."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:11
msgid ""
"For macOS, you can download it from zed.dev/download, or install via "
"Homebrew:"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:17
msgid ""
"For Windows, download the installer from zed.dev/download, or install via "
"winget:"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:23
msgid ""
"For most Linux users, the easiest way to install Zed is through our "
"installation script:"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:29
msgid ""
"After installation, you can launch Zed from your Applications folder "
"(macOS), Start menu (Windows), or directly from the terminal using: `zed .` "
"This opens the current directory in Zed."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:33
msgid "Set Up the JetBrains Keymap"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:35
msgid ""
"If you're coming from RustRover, the fastest way to feel at home is to use "
"the JetBrains keymap. During onboarding, you can select it as your base "
"keymap. If you missed that step, you can change it anytime:"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:37 src/migrate/rustrover.md:359
msgid "Open Settings with `Cmd+,` (macOS) or `Ctrl+,` (Linux/Windows)"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:38
msgid "Search for `Base Keymap`"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:39
msgid "Select `JetBrains`"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:41
msgid ""
"This maps familiar shortcuts like `Shift Shift` for Search Everywhere, "
"`Cmd+O` for Go to Class, and `Cmd+Shift+A` for Find Action."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:43
msgid "Set Up Editor Preferences"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:45
msgid ""
"You can configure most settings in the Settings Editor (<kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">cmd-,|ctrl-,</kbd>). For advanced settings, run `zed: "
"open settings file` from the Command Palette to edit your settings file "
"directly."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:47
msgid "Settings RustRover users typically configure first:"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:49
msgid "Zed Setting"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:49
msgid "What it does"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:51
msgid "`format_on_save`"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:51
msgid ""
"Auto-format when saving. Set to `\"on\"` to enable (uses rustfmt by default)."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:52
msgid "`soft_wrap`"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:52
msgid ""
"Wrap long lines. Options: `\"none\"`, `\"editor_width\"`, "
"`\"preferred_line_length\"`"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:53
msgid "`preferred_line_length`"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:53
msgid "Column width for wrapping and rulers. Rust convention is 100."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:54
msgid "`inlay_hints`"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:54
msgid "Show type hints, parameter names, and chaining hints inline."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:55
msgid "`relative_line_numbers`"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:55
msgid "Useful if you're coming from IdeaVim."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:57
msgid ""
"Zed also supports per-project settings. Create a `.zed/settings.json` file "
"in your project root to override global settings for that project."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:59
msgid ""
"**Tip:** If you're joining an existing project, check `format_on_save` "
"before making your first commit. Otherwise you might accidentally reformat "
"an entire file when you only meant to change one line."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:61
msgid "Open or Create a Project"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:63
msgid ""
"After setup, press `Cmd+Shift+O` (with JetBrains keymap) to open a folder. "
"This becomes your workspace in Zed."
msgstr ""

