#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:144
msgid "Differences in User Interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:146
msgid "Different Analysis Engines"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:148
msgid ""
"RustRover uses its own proprietary code analysis engine for Rust "
"intelligence. Zed uses rust-analyzer via the Language Server Protocol (LSP)."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:150
msgid "What this means for you:"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:152
msgid ""
"**Completions, go-to-definition, find usages, type inference** — All "
"available in Zed via rust-analyzer"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:153
msgid "**Macro expansion** — Available in both (use `Cmd+Shift+M` in Zed)"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:154
msgid ""
"**Inlay hints** — Both support type hints, parameter hints, and chaining "
"hints"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:156
msgid "Where you might notice differences:"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:158
msgid ""
"Some refactorings available in RustRover may not have rust-analyzer "
"equivalents"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:159
msgid "RustRover-specific inspections (beyond Clippy) won't exist in Zed"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:160
msgid "rust-analyzer is configured via JSON in Zed, not through a GUI"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/rustrover.md:162 src/migrate/rustrover.md:180
